READING: genuine=0 columns are where the mod-p reduction CAN power a char-0 proof
(d = p^k pattern); nonzero genuine cells are the obstruction — the landscape maps
exactly which (d,p) reductions are usable. First open char-0 degrees (literature:
12, 20, 24, ... UNVERIFIED citation) need a p with genuine=0 — the table shows
whether any small p qualifies for d=8 etc. NEXT: extend d=9..12 with sampling +
the p-adic lifting criterion (Graf von Bothmer et al. route) on the zero cells.
